  "description": "PARADOX — A Hackathon in the Madness of the Multiverse PARADOX is an 8-hour hackathon that brings together innovation, technology, creativity, and problem-solving. Inspired by the concept of a multiverse, the event challenges participants to explore different possibilities and transform their ideas into practical solutions. The event is organized in collaboration with three IEEE societies — IEEE ComSoc, IEEE APS, and IEEE WIE — bringing together diverse technical communities under one platform. Participants will work in teams to understand a given problem statement, brainstorm innovative approaches, build their solution within the limited time, and present their final work to the judging panel. Eligibility: Open to college students Team: Inter-college and inter-specialization teams are allowed Format: Multiple rounds including ideation, development, and final presentation Evaluation: Innovation, startup scope, technical implementation, feasibility, impact, and presentation Mode: Offline Duration: An intense 8-hour hackathon (Phase 2 : 9 am - 5 pm)",
