    "details": "<p><strong>PARADOX &mdash; A Hackathon in the Madness of the Multiverse</strong></p>\n<p>PARADOX is an 8-hour hackathon that brings together innovation, technology, creativity, and problem-solving. Inspired by the concept of a multiverse, the event challenges participants to explore different possibilities and transform their ideas into practical solutions.</p>\n<p>The event is organized in collaboration with three IEEE societies &mdash; IEEE ComSoc, IEEE APS, and IEEE WIE &mdash; bringing together diverse technical communities under one platform.</p>\n<p>Participants will work in teams to understand a given problem statement, brainstorm innovative approaches, build their solution within the limited time, and present their final work to the judging panel.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Eligibility:</strong> Open to college students</li>\n<li><strong>Team:</strong> Inter-college and inter-specialization teams are allowed</li>\n<li><strong>Format:</strong> Multiple rounds including ideation, development, and final presentation</li>\n<li><strong>Evaluation:</strong> Innovation, startup scope, technical implementation, feasibility, impact, and presentation</li>\n<li><strong>Mode:</strong> Offline</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong> An intense 8-hour hackathon (Phase 2 : 9 am - 5 pm)</li>\n</ul>",
